From 4880cf6e1d3f2135cb9269bb51c01af88a4e4b98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sak-114514 <Sak-114514@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:47:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Keep the DFlash trial within the measured V100 memory
 margin

The depth-four candidate met the single-stream throughput and short-request
four-way targets, but a 0.95 memory fraction OOMed on four 16k requests.
The 0.94 fraction retained a 64k single request and 30-minute four-way 1k
stability without that OOM, so the isolated launcher now defaults to it.
Document the observed concurrency limit and the exact-norm A/B tradeoff.

Constraint: Three 16GB V100s and an opt-in 64k DFlash2 trial
Rejected: 0.95 utilization | four 16k requests triggered CUDA OOM
Rejected: Native exact gated norm | fixed one near-tie output but lost four-way 1k admission
Confidence: medium
Scope-risk: narrow
Reversibility: clean
Directive: Do not infer four-way long-context capacity from the short-request stability result
Tested: 1804s four-way 1k run at 0.94 with 1311 successful requests; 64k greedy request; 16k four-way pilot; shell syntax and git diff check
Not-tested: Four simultaneous full-64k contexts; production switch; full-project CI
---
 tools/ac922/README.md          | 15 ++++++++++-----
 tools/ac922/serve_tp3_trial.sh |  4 ++--
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/ac922/README.md b/tools/ac922/README.md
index 445bf4c11..3bfe822a6 100644
--- a/tools/ac922/README.md
+++ b/tools/ac922/README.md
@@ -70,12 +70,17 @@ sh tools/ac922/serve_tp3_trial.sh dflash
 ```
 
 The baseline defaults to a 200k window and 0.90 GPU utilization. The DFlash2
-mode defaults to a 64k window, depth 3, 0.93 utilization, and four schedulable
-requests. Override with `AC922_MAX_MODEL_LEN`, `AC922_DFLASH_DEPTH`, or
+trial defaults to a 64k window, depth 4, and 0.94 utilization. Override with
+`AC922_MAX_MODEL_LEN`, `AC922_DFLASH_DEPTH`, or
 `AC922_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION` for experiments. Depth 7 achieved higher
-single-stream decode speed, while the measured four-way configuration uses
-depth 3 and a five-group KV layout. Four simultaneous full-64k requests do
-not fit in the measured KV pool.
+single-stream decode speed, but could not schedule four 1k requests. Depth 4
+at 0.95 passed a 30-minute four-way 1k trial, then CUDA-OOMed on four 16k
+prompts. At 0.94, four 1k requests ran without waiting and a 64k request
+completed; four 16k requests completed without OOM but only three ran at once.
+Four simultaneous full-64k requests do not fit in the measured KV pool.
+The optional native exact gated-norm path corrected one near-tie greedy
+divergence in an A/B run, but reduced the KV pool enough to prevent four
+simultaneous 1k requests; it is therefore not enabled by this launcher.
 
 `compare_greedy_tp2_tp3.py` captures and compares deterministic output token
 IDs. `bench_stream_token_ids.py` counts token IDs inside streamed chunks;
diff --git a/tools/ac922/serve_tp3_trial.sh b/tools/ac922/serve_tp3_trial.sh
index df42ef47a..578e29d4d 100755
--- a/tools/ac922/serve_tp3_trial.sh
+++ b/tools/ac922/serve_tp3_trial.sh
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ set -eu
 mode=${1:-baseline}
 case "$mode" in
     baseline) default_len=200000; default_util=0.90 ;;
-    dflash) default_len=65536; default_util=0.93 ;;
+    dflash) default_len=65536; default_util=0.94 ;;
     *) echo "usage: $0 baseline|dflash" >&2; exit 2 ;;
 esac
 model=${AC922_MODEL_PATH:-/home/debian/models/qwen3.8-27b-awq-nicosuter}
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ case "$mode" in
         test -d "$draft"
         export VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1
         export AC922_TP3_DFLASH_REPLICATE=1
-        depth=${AC922_DFLASH_DEPTH:-3}
+        depth=${AC922_DFLASH_DEPTH:-4}
         case "$depth" in 1|2|3|4|5|6|7) ;; *) echo "invalid DFlash depth" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
         spec="{\"method\":\"dflash\",\"model\":\"$draft\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":$depth,\"draft_tensor_parallel_size\":3,\"draft_sample_method\":\"probabilistic\",\"kv_cache_dtype\":\"auto\"}"
         set -- "$@" --speculative-config "$spec"
-- 
